  "description": "Contract checks for Model Context Protocol servers, run from any test framework. McpContract connects as a client and reports what a model would trip over: no title or instructions, the product never named, tools and prompts without descriptions or annotations, enumerations and ranges written in prose instead of the schema, long dashes, errors returned as success, crashes passed off as refusals, the SDK's generic error text, escaped non-Latin text, answers over budget, structured content that breaks its own output schema and instructions naming tools that are gone. McpTestServer runs any server in memory. Works with servers built on the bare C# SDK or on TechTeaStudio.Mcp. Targets net6.0 through net11.0.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
